# pc_sound_split.wrap: the MusyX calls the game exe is linked with --wrap=<name> for (port/tools/firstlink.py reads
# this list). The sound split prototype (pc_sound_split.c, docs/port/sound-split.md) gives each to both MusyX
# instances; with ORRE_SOUND_SPLIT off, each wrapper only calls the real function with the same arguments.
# Only calls that change the sound are listed: calls that ask (sndFXCheck, sndSeqGetValid, sndCheckEmitter,
# sndIsInstalled) and the movies' streams (sndStream*) stay the game instance's alone.
sndInit
sndQuit
sndSetHooks
sndSetSampleDataUploadCallback
sndPushGroup
sndSetAuxProcessingCallbacks
sndAuxCallbackPrepareReverbHI
sndAuxCallbackUpdateSettingsReverbHI
sndOutputMode
sndMasterVolume
sndVolume
sndFXStartEx
sndFXCtrl
sndFXKeyOff
sndSeqPlayEx
sndSeqStop
sndSeqContinue
sndSeqVolume
sndAddEmitter
s3dSetListener
s3dUpdateListener
